# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code machine-local settings (not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Large and raw artifacts live in $TROPICAL_SCRATCH, never in the repo:
# the AI Hub subtropical image cache (h4_img256.npy, ~8 GB) and the
# redistribution-prohibited CDD dataset (raw imagery + raw environment series). Only scripts and imagery-free
# derived metadata (small CSV/parquet) are versioned. Guard against an accidental
# commit if TROPICAL_SCRATCH is ever mis-pointed at the repo tree.
*.npy
# The CDD per-image record (labels, crops, diseases, photo dates and times) is the
# competition's data, which its rules forbid redistributing. dacon_granularity.py
# writes it to $TROPICAL_SCRATCH; this guard keeps it out of the repository if
# TROPICAL_SCRATCH ever points into the tree.
dacon_meta.parquet

# Third-party material consulted while coding the cited studies and analyzing the two
# datasets -- the articles read, the dataset documentation the providers supply --
# is not kept in this tree at all. SOURCES.md carries the route to each and nothing
# else: the data-availability statement ships derivations rather than other people's
# material, and the AI Hub terms restrict redistribution of what its provider
# supplies, so committing either contradicts a section the paper stands on.

# Internal working documents -- a claim ledger, a coverage matrix, a fact-check
# report -- are not part of the released tree. Ignore the directory, never the
# filenames: a filename ignored per report is a membership list, and the next
# report is not on it.
_internal/

# LaTeX build artifacts (regenerated by `latexmk -cd -pdf paper/main.tex`), in any
# directory.
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.spl
*.synctex.gz
*-eps-converted-to.pdf
paper/main.pdf
paper/supplementary.pdf
